      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T16:39:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See [this doc](https://source.android.com/docs/security/features/selinux/concepts#security_contexts). TL;DR, it\u0027s part of the SELinux label of a file, in addition to the file type, to indicate which app and human user own the file.\n\nThis comment aims to explain why we don\u0027t do a second-round restorecon like what we do in `dexopt`, so it should be looked at together with [the comment in `dexopt`](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/artd/artd.cc;l\u003d1160-1165;drc\u003d9a36de50228fdff9ed53e1dd9545eb446ed09943).",
